      "id": "0a6e078f-73f7-42a6-9272-c6254f4222e1",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "3. Hexadecimal, including fractions",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "7e4c9ea0-9451-4ac0-8b7e-6f03ba35783a",
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "7e86764a-353e-4b9a-9c2b-0aeaeabedf63",
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "306c2d70-d7a0-4134-bb40-4d841072b4a5",
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "id": "84281fb0-4a2b-4d65-be19-19540b040304",
      "text": "Each hexadecimal digit corresponds to exactly four bits because $16=2^4$. A\u2013F represent decimal 10\u201315.\n\nStart at the radix point and group outward. Add leading zeroes on the integer side or trailing zeroes on the fraction side; never insert padding next to the radix point.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "7e4c9ea0-9451-4ac0-8b7e-6f03ba35783a",
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "columns": [
        "Hex",
        "Binary",
        "Hex",
        "Binary"
      ],
      "id": "645d309f-0b6c-43f1-83ff-e24508deb889",
      "rows": [
        [
          "0",
          "0000",
          "8",
          "1000"
        ],
        [
          "1",
          "0001",
